  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1231 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThe dog days of summer continue through the end of July. The core of \nstrong subtropical ridging will wander around the Texas Panhandle \nand New Mexico through the week. As conditions remain dry and the \nairmass warms, near surface humidity should mix out more and allow \ndaytime highs to inch upwards into the triple digits. Outside of the \nslightly cooler higher elevations in the Hill Country, most of South \nCentral Texas is forecast to see multiple days of 100F+ highs this \nweek. Overnight lows will stay around the mid to upper 70s. This \ncombination may lead to rising heat risks through the week.\n\nThe forecast through at least Friday stays dry for essentially \neveryone in the local area. However, there is good model agreement \nthat the core of the subtropical ridge will slowly saunter a little \nmore west this upcoming weekend. Northerly flow through the Plains \nand increased troughiness could support some low end rain chances \nduring the weekend, though the moisture supply does not look \nespecially plentiful at this time.",
